  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Here en = ethylene diamine&nbsp;</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/d860c86f-474f-49fd-9f86-76feafc2b9f5-9894773.png\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 328px;\" /></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;[PtCl<sub>2</sub>(en)<sub>2</sub>]<sup>2+</sup>&nbsp;forms cis and trans-isomers. Only the cis-isomers has no element of symmetry.&nbsp;So it is optically active. Trans&nbsp;- [PtCl<sub>2</sub>(en)<sub>2</sub>]<sup>2+</sup>&nbsp;form is optically inactive. Square planar complexes doesn&#39;t exhibit optical isomerism.</p>",
